{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381806-where-the-fuck-is-utahi","id":1381806,"title":"Where the fuck is Utahi?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-15T16:57:55-07:00","id":1381806,"title":"Where the fuck is Utahi?","content":"I'm having a blast reading the most recent preview of Heirs of the Shogunate and especially the War in the West section, but with so many locales new and old involved I'm having a really hard time pinpointing where anything is, and the 3rd edition map isn't helping. An-Teng is loosely labeled, I assume Zhaojun is around where Goldenseal is, and I guess the Meiyu Coast is somewhere in between? According to 2nd edition maps Abalone is the big island southernmost of Wavecrest, so I guess Utahi is the one immediately north? Where does the Wavecrest Archipielago end and The Neck begin?<br /> <br /> Also what the fuck is a Randan? it's marked down on the map yet I haven't been able to find a single mention of it across the Core, Dragon-Blooded and The Realm.<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping we get a new map with the full Companion Book's release, but in the meantime can anyone help a fellow ST sort out this mess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T16:59:30-07:00","id":1381808,"title":"","content":"Apparently there will be multiple maps in Across Eight Directions, so hopefully that helps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:24:59-07:00","id":1381818,"title":"","content":"the Meiyu Sea is that almost inland sea in front of Goldenseal, the Baihi city states, they are directly north of Goldenseal, around the Meiyu Sea's opening, where that fang-like peninsula and the two islands near it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:37:03-07:00","id":1381822,"title":"","content":"As for Wavecrest and the Neck, essentially in past editions Wavecrest was basically just those two chunky islands at the bottom of the chain. Same with Coral, its basically the big island in the north and everything north/east. So the Neck is basically all those small islands in between.<br /> <br /> And yeah we are gonna be getting some maps in the At8D. I believe one per Direction? each very detailed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:57:01-07:00","id":1381827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381806-where-the-fuck-is-utahi#post1381806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also what the fuck is a Randan? it's marked down on the map yet I haven't been able to find a single mention of it across the Core, Dragon-Blooded and The Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div> Basically it got cut from the core, there's a character from there who was mentioned in Eric Minton's blog. Her backstory alluded to a prestigious weaver's lodge that's capable of creating enchanted garments.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T18:06:41-07:00","id":1381830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381806-where-the-fuck-is-utahi#post1381806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a blast reading the most recent preview of Heirs of the Shogunate and especially the War in the West section, but with so many locales new and old involved I'm having a really hard time pinpointing where anything is, and the 3rd edition map isn't helping. An-Teng is loosely labeled, I assume Zhaojun is around where Goldenseal is, and I guess the Meiyu Coast is somewhere in between? According to 2nd edition maps Abalone is the big island southernmost of Wavecrest, so I guess Utahi is the one immediately north? Where does the Wavecrest Archipielago end and The Neck begin?<br /> <br /> Also what the fuck is a Randan? it's marked down on the map yet I haven't been able to find a single mention of it across the Core, Dragon-Blooded and The Realm.<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping we get a new map with the full Companion Book's release, but in the meantime can anyone help a fellow ST sort out this mess?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really a \u201cmess\u201d. Just the new normal of continuously dropping references to the countless nations, cultures, and locals throughout Creation every chance they get to hammer in how vast the world is, and those blank spaces on the map is occupied by many many more cultures. Some of these places may get explored in A8D, but as they do, there will inevitably be dropped references to their unexplored neighbors, so they never fall in 2E\u2019s rut of never adding to Creation and only deep delving on a finite list of locals with vast emptiness in between","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T11:54:00-07:00","id":1381955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381806-where-the-fuck-is-utahi?p=1381830#post1381830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really a \u201cmess\u201d. Just the new normal of continuously dropping references to the countless nations, cultures, and locals throughout Creation every chance they get to hammer in how vast the world is, and those blank spaces on the map is occupied by many many more cultures. Some of these places may get explored in A8D, but as they do, there will inevitably be dropped references to their unexplored neighbors, so they never fall in 2E\u2019s rut of never adding to Creation and only deep delving on a finite list of locals with vast emptiness in between</div> </div> </div> </div>They could do this while giving more guidance about what places are where. However, there's no one great way to do this and it's unclear how helpful they would be.<br /> <br /> It guess it's impractical to make a new large map giving all the locations for every book, or small maps for each individual location, but they could include verbal descriptions. <br /> <br /> However when they just define something by a brief reference they might want to be intentionally ambiguous with the location to leave room for more ideas later, that might require it to be on water or off it (or whatever). For places with substantial writeups I imagine this is not as much of a problem, but there still may be reasons to maintain some strategic ambiguity.<br /> <br /> One part of the solution would be to, whenever they draw a map, include a bunch of named locations they don't have writeups for yet, and match new writeups they come up with to these locations. Unfortunately this approach leads to the other type of confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T18:57:56-07:00","id":1382030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381806-where-the-fuck-is-utahi?p=1381822#post1381822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Wavecrest and the Neck, essentially in past editions Wavecrest was basically just those two chunky islands at the bottom of the chain. Same with Coral, its basically the big island in the north and everything north/east. So the Neck is basically all those small islands in between.<br /> <br /> And yeah we are gonna be getting some maps in the At8D. I believe one per Direction? each very detailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor correction: the Neck is a small group of those in between islands just south of the Skullstone archipelago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T04:01:54-07:00","id":1382313,"title":"","content":"In our group, we decided that the map in the corebook is loosely canonical and as accurate as any really old map, so no one should be surprised if amidst a long journey, they encounter some see they cannot easily identify.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T04:16:14-07:00","id":1382314,"title":"","content":"A very important way to do it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T04:17:58-07:00","id":1382315,"title":"","content":"Anyway, I imagine that Across the Eight Directions will include maps with more locations included. If they included all the locations on the Core map, it'd get messy. But a map of just the Western islands could include a lot more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T02:07:14-07:00","id":1444612,"title":"","content":"Necroposting here but if I may &quot;What the fuck is Utahi&quot; ? I'm trying to do a setting around here and I can't find any reference for it in the Lunar book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T02:49:44-07:00","id":1444619,"title":"","content":"For half a second misread the title as &quot;Where the fuck is Utah?&quot; and was both amused and confused by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T03:05:27-07:00","id":1444621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381806-where-the-fuck-is-utahi?p=1444612#post1444612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Necroposting here but if I may &quot;What the fuck is Utahi&quot; ? I'm trying to do a setting around here and I can't find any reference for it in the Lunar book</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the writeup is in The Realm, pages 175 to 177.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T03:13:57-07:00","id":1444622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381806-where-the-fuck-is-utahi?p=1444621#post1444621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the writeup is in The Realm, pages 175 to 177.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks ! (a lot, mandatory 10 characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T03:32:10-07:00","id":1444623,"title":"","content":"So I'm coming with a second question : What is the Neck Archipelago ? Because Utahn is supposed to be as the southernmost of the Neck Archipelago, but just North of Utahi is Brightwork, which is apparently in the Auspiscene archipelago, so am I missing something ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T04:40:20-07:00","id":1444627,"title":"","content":"IIRC The Neck is the name of that whole band of islands between Coral and Wavecrest. So I would say the Auspiscene is a geographically distinct grouping of islands within the very, very large group called &quot;The Neck&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or, perhaps more interstingly, maybe the two groups of islands are offset from one another at an angle? So the southern end of one stretches &quot;under&quot; the northern end of the other? Like: //","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-19-2021, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T05:44:43-07:00","id":1444634,"title":"","content":"So if I understand properly, &quot;The Neck&quot; is actually the whole chain of islands from South to North on the West ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:50:13-07:00","id":1444663,"title":"","content":"Utahi is on the map in <i>Lunars</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T17:24:26-07:00","id":1444733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381806-where-the-fuck-is-utahi?p=1444634#post1444634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I understand properly, &quot;The Neck&quot; is actually the whole chain of islands from South to North on the West ?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is from 2E, but as I said before: the Neck is a group of those islands.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://suptg.thisisnotatrueending.com/qstarchive/1512842/thumbs/1496326166237.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","us